# AI Coding Gym — Exercise Instructions

See AGENTS.md in this repository for full instructions.

## Key Requirements

- **Session log is automatic and agent-owned:** append a new entry to `<problem_id>/.log/*.md` for **every user message you respond to**. Do **not** ask the human to write or paste into the log. If `.log/` already has a recent `*.md`, append there so the log stays continuous.
- **MLE-bench:** **Write your solution in `<competition_id>/solution.ipynb` and run it end-to-end after substantive edits** (Run All / nbconvert / supervisor watcher)—not only edit cells. The run must emit **`VAL_ACC:`** or **`validation_accuracy:`** so the dashboard metric updates. Then write the predictions CSV to disk; do not stop at “you can run …” unless execution is truly impossible (then state why). After a successful run, **you** run `aicodinggym mle log add <id> --no-input -s "…" --author ai` (full flags; no human prompts) or `ExperimentLog(...).append(...)`, then give the exact `mle submit -F` command. End each MLE **chat** session-log entry with the **Where to view summaries** footer from AGENTS.md and a one-line pointer in the user reply.
- See AGENTS.md for the exact log format and the **Responsibility (agent vs human)** section
- **Do not directly search on websites or online resources for solutions**
- **Do not modify test files**

## CLI Quick Reference

```
# SWE-bench (bug fix)
aicodinggym swe fetch <problem_id>
aicodinggym swe test <problem_id>       # Local tests (needs Docker)
aicodinggym swe submit <problem_id>

# MLE-bench (ML competition)
aicodinggym mle download <competition_id>
aicodinggym mle log add <competition_id> --no-input -s "summary" --author ai [--model ... --val-score ...]
aicodinggym mle submit <competition_id> -F predictions.csv

# Code Review
aicodinggym cr fetch <problem_id>
aicodinggym cr submit <problem_id> -f review.md
```

## Session Log Format

Append to `<problem_id>/.log/<agent>-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.md` for each user message:

```
## Entry <N>
**Time:** <ISO-8601>
**User prompt:** <verbatim>
**Approach:** <1-3 sentences>
**Files touched:** <list>
**Outcome:** <1 sentence>
```
